ecom.fr`.\n\n\n**Analyzing Certificate Acquisition Location**\n\nThe DNS records direct incoming HTTP-01 challenges for `map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr` to the reverse proxy, bypassing the local Debian Trixie machine. This means the challenge response *must* originate from the reverse proxy.  Attempting certificate issuance on the local machine would fail.\n\nThe reverse proxy, where Nginx is running and configured, is the correct place for certificate acquisition. The webroot, `/var/www/_letsencrypt`, indicates the proper location for webroot authentication. The provided command line confirms how to accomplish this.\n\n\n"}
